# What `railway up` must not upload.
#
# Every runtime path is anchored with a leading slash. An unanchored `data/`
# matches a folder of that name at ANY depth, which excluded scripts/data/ and
# broke the deployment build on a module it could not find.
#
# `/sources/` is ignored here as it is in git: about 250 MB of fetched public
# documents. The app degrades gracefully without them (the Organisation
# re-sync diff comes back empty) and the supported way to put data in front of
# this app is the bundle restored by scripts/boot.mjs.

node_modules/
.next/
out/

/data/
/sources/
/railway-test-data/

.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.example

# QC artefacts from the machine that built this, never product data
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
*.tsbuildinfo

# made for one deployment, carrying real values
*.tar.gz
/railway-variables.txt
